  "result": "I added `percent(part, total)` in `src/core/percent.ts` and committed it as `4c8d2b6`. `npm run fast` passed.\n\n- **Behaviour:** it returns one decimal, so `percent(1, 3)` gives `33.3%`, and `0.0%` when the total is zero.\n- **Helpers:** I found nothing in `src/` to reuse, so it is a single expression with no imports, which also keeps core independent of adapters.\n- **Tests:** `test/core/percent.test.ts` uses node:test and covers the one-decimal rendering and the zero-total case.\n- **Shard weight:** I gave the new test a weight of 0.1 in `scripts/lib/shard-weights.mjs`. That number is a guess, not a measured time.\n- **Commit title:** the repo convention says to end the title with the task id in parentheses. No task id was in the brief, so the title has none. If you give me the id, I can amend the commit.",
